{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1214373-the-lodge-of-the-hook-hand","id":1214373,"title":"The Lodge of the Hook Hand","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-02T17:54:28-07:00","id":1214373,"title":"The Lodge of the Hook Hand","content":"<b>The Lodge of the Hook Hand</b><br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Scarecrows, Leatherfaces, Spooks<br /> <i>\u201cI wouldn\u2019t go out in those woods tonight, the Barclay Butcher prowls them on the nights of the full moon. I know you kids think he\u2019s just an urban legend, but trust me, you\u2019re going to meet him if you don\u2019t listen to me.\u201d</i><br /> It is often said that fear is the oldest, most primal emotion of mankind. Even though we long ago erased \u201cHere there be dragons\u201d from the unexplored corners of our maps, we have never ceased to believe that monsters lurk just outside the boundaries of our everyday lives: in the shadows, in the woods, in the neighborhoods we avoid walking through at night. The Lodge of the Hook Hand knows that this instinct of humankind-- the drive to create scary stories and urban legends\u2014is one of the most valuable weapons in the Hunt and they wield it like a subtle knife, using terrifying tales to protect the Herd from the very real horrors that lurk beyond their ken.<br /> The Lodge of the Hook Hand has its roots in rural West Virginia, deep in the woods of Appalachia. Jeremiah \u201cScreaming Terror\u201d McCabe was a Hunter in Darkness Cahalith whose pack had the misfortune of having a <i>magath</i> take up residence on their territory. The spirit, a twisted creature born of essence of death, pain, love, and lust, had begun stalking the local lovers\u2019 lane, driving young couples to kill each other in brutal, sexual murder-suicides. McCabe\u2019s pack attempted to put down the <i>magath</i>, but the spirit being was powerful and McCabe\u2019s pack was small; McCabe ended up being the only survivor of the battle and the <i>magath </i>was still on the loose.<br /> Unable to defeat the <i>magath</i> through conventional means, McCabe was forced to resort to unconventional methods. McCabe, given his nature as a Cahalith, had always been a tale-teller by nature; from that talent, he began to hatch a plan. He began spreading rumors that an escaped maniac with a hook for a hand had taken up residence near the lovers\u2019 lane and that he was the one who was responsible for the killings. Few believed McCabe at first, but the wily Cahalith began staging encounters with the Hook Hand Killer, sneaking up on unsuspecting young couples in Dalu, dressed in a dark coat with a wicked-looking hook as a weapon. Between the ingrained seed of fear he\u2019d planted and Lunacy, the teens he frightened off began to believe the myths of the Hook Hand and started avoiding the lovers\u2019 lane. The <i>magath,</i> suddenly starved of essence, tried to move to new hunting grounds in the area, but the Hook Hand followed it. Eventually, the <i>magath </i>grew tired of working for its food and left the area, leaving McCabe victorious in a certain fashion. Soon, other Hunters in the area heard tell of his clever plot and came to him, asking for tutelage.<br /> Most of the Lodge of the Hook Hand are Cahalith Hunters in Darkness, just like its founder. In fact, the Lodge currently only considers Hunters in Darkness for membership. The Hunters, being so intimately tied to their territory, are the werewolves most suited to setting up the mock-horror movie scenarios that the Lodge\u2019s tactics rely on. A few Rahu and Irraka have joined the lodge over the years, but Cahalith, with their natural talents for inspiring fear in their prey and spreading tales, make up the vast majority of the Lodge.<br /> In broader Uratha society, the Lodge of the Hook Hand is viewed as an interesting, if creepy, group of eccentrics. Few can deny that their unorthodox methods of protecting their territories work, but find their obsession with causing fear and terror slightly creepy. The slim minority of Hook Hands who end up completely losing themselves to their stories and begin killing anyone who intrudes on their territory does little to improve their reputation.<br /> The Lodge of the Hook Hand maintains an informal rivalry with the Lodge of the Screaming Moon with the two Lodges often having competitions to see whether one can scare the other.<br /> <b>Totem: Bloody-Handed-Horror</b><br /> Bloody-Handed-Horror is a powerful fear spirit that grew by feeding on the resonance of terror from slasher movies in the 1970s and 80s. It takes the form of a massive humanoid figure with a hockey mask for a face and machetes for hands.<br /> Bloody-Handed-Horror was approached by the Lodge of the Hook Hand soon after its initial foundation in the 1970s. While the spirit was not as powerful then as it is now, the Lodge believed that the spirit\u2019s resonance with modern-day horror stories would help them in inspiring the sort of fear portrayed in slasher movies in real life. Bloody-Handed-Horror, for it\u2019s part, was all-too-happy to help in spreading the sort of fear that it had grown fat on move from the silver screen into the real world.<br /> Bloody-Handed-Horror is an unusually attentive totem for a Lodge. Despite his nature as a spirit of fear, his demeanor is that of a doting and supportive father to his adoptive children. He often offers advice on how a given Scarecrow might develop his legend to be more effective, or at the very least more interesting. Many members of the Lodge think that spending so much time around movie theaters as a young spirit has given their totem an interest in screenwriting (or at least screenwriting as a spirit understands it).<br /> <b>Bonds</b><br /> <b>Blessing: </b>The blessing of the Lodge of the Hook Hand subtly twists the way Lunacy works on its victims. When viewing the werewolf in a form that would normally inspire Lunacy, a mortal who fails their Lunacy roll will believe that he saw the legendary figure that the Lodge member portrays. If they dramatically fail the roll, they become wolf-blooded as usual.<br /> <b>Aspiration: </b>To frighten those who invade their territory.<br /> <b>Bane: </b>A member of the Lodge must spread their legend when given the chance to.<br /> <b>Sacred Hunt:</b><br /> The Lodge\u2019s Sacred Hunt gives the hunter instinctive general knowledge of where their prey is on their territory. A lodge member knows how many intruders are on their territory at any given time, and knows the general direction they are from them. They do not have a know the exact location of their prey, but the prey gains a -2 to stealth rolls to hide from the werewolf. Hook Hands have a deep connection to their hunting grounds, even for a werewolves, and their hunts often involve herding intruders off of their lands through terror or driving them into a choke point where the rest of their pack will be laying in wait.<br /> <b>Tools</b><br /> The Lodge of the Hook Hand has access to the Lodge Lorehouse and Lodge Sorcery merits, and may choose influences from Fear, Death, and Inspiration.<br /> <b>Witch Whisper (Two Dot Fetish)</b><br /> This fetish typically takes the form of the skull of a small animal tied to a leather cord. It is usually imbued with a spirit of fear or courage.<br /> Effect:<br /> The user faces the target so that the fetishes eyeholes are pointing towards them and activates it. When the user puts the fetish to their ear, the spirit inside will whisper the target\u2019s greatest fear to the user. The user learns the subject\u2019s fear as well as any tilts or conditions associated with it. A single Witch Whisper can only hold a single subject\u2019s fear at a time, but some more dramatic members of the lodge where garlands of Witch Whispers so they can learn the fears of large groups of people at once.<br /> <b>Monster Claw (Three Dot Fetish)</b><br /> A Monster Claw is a fetish taking the form of a large claw of a bear, wolf, or great cat, or a large thorn. A spirit of fear or death is bound to this fetish.<br /> Effect:<br /> This fetish is activated by scraping the claw across the users palm. If it is successfully activated, the user\u2019s mouth and fingers or claws begin to drip with blood. The sight of this blood inspires the primordial fear of the Monster in any mortal who witnesses it. While this fetish is activated, the user can target a single target and roll Presence+Intimidate as a reflexive action. On a successful roll, the target receives the Frightened condition for the duration of the scene. On an exceptional success, they also gain the Shaken Condition. The blood produced by this fetish disappears at the end of the scene and cannot be used to sustain vampires or any other creature that feeds on blood.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23991-bacchicone","name":"BacchicOne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23991_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T18:29:08-07:00","id":1214384,"title":"","content":"Hmmmm...crossover potential with the Begotten and the changeling Scarecrow Ministry Entitlement...!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key